_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:197:Whether storyboard images and animation assets are mutually exclusive, combinable, or selectable per scene must be encoded in the Assemble Project adapter contract **after auditing the existing assembly logic** (Phase 0).
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:377:    adapters/
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:382:Adapters call stable service functions. If pipeline step functions are too route-coupled to reuse safely, **extract shared service functions without changing existing endpoint behavior**, then have both the fixed pipeline and workflow adapters call them. Do not make workflow adapters call Flask routes over HTTP from inside the same process.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:394:Compute a node fingerprint from a canonical representation of: node type + version, relevant configuration, resolved inputs and upstream artifact fingerprints, and adapter/cache schema version.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:454:Extract reusable services where route-bound pipeline steps require it; adapters for core production nodes; deterministic scheduler + per-project locking; execution record persistence; full-workflow, single-node-with-dependencies, and **isolated single-node (stub-fed) runs with sample-derived markers**; sequenced SSE events; live canvas states, logs, summaries, errors, stop; open generated projects in the existing timeline editor.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\proposition-final.md:497:- Registry metadata is authoritative, but adapters remain normal tested Python code; do not encode arbitrary executor logic in JSON.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:35:Resolve the open question: how Assemble treats storyboard images vs animation assets (audit `_step_assemble` at line 1919 and `_step_assets` at 1813) — encode the answer in the Assemble adapter contract.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:161:### 3.2 Node adapters
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:162:`studio/workflows/adapters/` wrapping the extracted services (tts, timing, segmenter, scenes, storyboard, animator, captions, music, assemble via editor, export) plus the trivial `project.setup` adapter (validate + emit settings). Adapters translate node inputs/config → service args, and service results → typed outputs + artifact refs; consumers of `project_settings` apply the explicit-beats-inherited rule (own config overrides incoming defaults). Extend the FFmpeg export engine with the **logo-overlay pass** (position/size/opacity/margin from settings, correct across all export profiles — same pattern as the grain overlay). Never call Flask routes over HTTP in-process.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:163:**Done when:** each adapter has a pytest exercising it against a fixture project (mock providers where needed); an export with logo enabled renders the watermark at the right position in 9:16, 16:9, and 1:1.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:190:`cache.py`: canonical fingerprint (type+version, relevant config, upstream artifact fingerprints, adapter schema version). Reuse only on fingerprint match + artifacts exist + integrity check + prior success + no forced regen. Edge/config/upstream changes mark descendants stale (orange). Persist cache-hit/miss reasons.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:196:- **Complete.** Canonical node fingerprints include resolved defaults, typed inputs, topology-qualified upstream output/artifact fingerprints, type version, and adapter cache schema version. Persistent cache entries are workflow/project/node scoped, atomic, and contain only component hashes plus reusable outputs.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:253:- Narration Only, Storyboard Only, and Re-export Existing Project are versioned, typed built-ins. All four built-in templates pass authoritative validation and execute successfully through the deterministic scheduler with adapter boundaries mocked.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:272:  cancellation, and the Story Generator adapter boundary.
_dev\loop-engineering\phases-plans\implementation-plan-old.md:283:  resolved values are schema-validated before fingerprinting and adapter execution.
